1	//! Findings: `findings.json`, the finding lifecycle and ratings.
2	//!
3	//! Mirrors the stored record `codex-findings.ps1` keeps (README "Findings: ids, status,
4	//! ratings"): the id `F<NN>-<k>` (`NN` the handoff number of the reply that raised it,
5	//! `k` its 1-based position in that reply's `findings[]`), the tracked `status`, the
6	//! severity, locations, the reviewer's claim/trigger/evidence, `supersedes`/`superseded_by`
7	//! bookkeeping, `source`, an append-only `history[]` (one entry per status change) and
8	//! `reviewer_checks[]` (one entry per later reply that reported on it). Field order matches
9	//! the on-disk record and is preserved by [`crate::ps_json`].
10	//!
11	//! [`transition`] is the pure status-change rule (README): `verified` requires evidence, a
12	//! `rejected` and a reopen (`-> proposed` from a non-`proposed` state) require a note, and
13	//! `superseded` requires neither; any status may follow any other. Acceptance test:
14	//! `tests/formats.rs` round-trips the real `.collab/c3-design/findings.json` byte-for-byte.
15	
16	use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
17	use serde_json::Value;
